ms"},{"effect":"May receive trauma-informed care, shelter, reintegration, and support services funded by the Department of State, and are explicitly protected from being sanctioned as perpetrators.","group":"Victims of human trafficking forced to work in online scam centers"},{"effect":"Required to participate in an interagency task force, share intelligence and data, coordinate implementation of the strategy, and submit regular reports to Congress.","group":"Federal agencies (Department of State, Department of Justice, Department of Homeland Security, Department of the Treasur"}],"key_provisions":["Requires the President to establish an interagency task force chaired by the Secretary of State within 30 days of enactment.","Mandates that the President evaluate 43 specified foreign persons and entities—along with any other responsible parties—for applicable sanctions under the Global Magnitsky Human Rights Accountability Act, the Trafficking Victims Protection Act of 2000, and Executive Order 13581.","Requires the task force to develop and submit a comprehensive U.S. strategy to Congress within 180 days to shut down online scam centers and dismantle criminal entities.","Authorizes the Department of State to provide trauma-informed care, shelter, reintegration, and support services for victims of trafficking within online scam centers.","Authorizes appropriations of $30 million for the Department of State for each of fiscal years 2026 and 2027 to develop, coordinate, and implement the strategy."],"missing_information":["Exact overall budgetary offsets or tax adjustments to fund the authorized appropriations.","Specific details on the exact outcomes if foreign governments refuse to cooperate with the task force beyond diplomatic pressure and sanctions."],"plain_summary":"The Dismantle Foreign Scam Syndicates Act requires the President to establish an interagency task force to shut down transnational criminal syndicates running mass online financial scams, such as 'pig butchering,' that target Americans and use forced labor in foreign scam centers. The bill mandates sanctions on specific foreign individuals and entities, authorizes support services for human trafficking victims, and authorizes appropriations of $30 million for the Department of State for fiscal years 2026 and 2027.","significance":"The bill creates a multi-agency federal response, mandates specific foreign sanctions, and authorizes funding and victim support programs to combat transnational online scam operations that have stolen billions of dollars from U.S. nationals."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-27T13:15:07+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5490/BILLS-119hr5490ih.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Dismantle Foreign Scam Syndicates Act","viability":51.4,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Committee hearing or markup"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":14.0,"value":0.4,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Markup / ordered reported"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":12.0,"value":0.8,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Floor activity","value":"Considered on the floor (rule, motion, cloture, vote)"}],"key":"floor","label":"Floor consideration","note":"","points":10.5,"value":0.7,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Days since latest action","value":327},{"label":"Half-life (days)","value":90}],"key":"momentum","label":"Recent action","note":"","points":1.21,"value":0.0806,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":10.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Cosponsors","value":72},{"label":"House majority","value":218}],"key":"cosponsors","label"